What it covers
--------------
Everything in this content/ folder: the lesson sources (src/: units, sentences, texts, dialogues, meanings, word-list
sources, the pronunciation lists), the generated lessons (packs/), the id lock, the audio settings (voices.json,
audio-overrides.json, pronunciations.json) and the schema. The app's code (everything outside content/) is MIT licensed:
see ../LICENSE.

You may share and adapt this material for non-commercial purposes, if you give appropriate credit ("Anzo lesson content
by Eduard Wichner, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", with a link to the licence), indicate if you made changes, and distribute your
contributions under the same licence. There is no warranty.

Why this licence: NT2Lex
------------------------
The level at which each Dutch word is taught is derived from NT2Lex, which is itself licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0:

  Tack, A., François, T., Desmet, P. & Fairon, C. (2018). NT2Lex: A CEFR-Graded Lexical Resource for Dutch as a
  Foreign Language Linked to Open Dutch WordNet. Proceedings of the 13th Workshop on Innovative Use of NLP for Building
  Educational Applications (BEA 2018). CENTAL (UCLouvain) / ITEC (KU Leuven). Licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

Derived from it: src/nl/wordlist-sources.yaml, src/nl/WORDLIST.md and the Dutch lessons built from them (src/nl/,
packs/nl/). Changes: Belgian standard Dutch forms and topic words added, words moved to other levels with a reason. The
whole content/ folder is published under the same licence, so the NT2Lex share-alike terms hold everywhere in it.

Other reference material
------------------------
The English, French and other Dutch levels follow official reference lists and sample papers (Cambridge English, France
Éducation international, CNaVT, Naar Nederland, Staatsexamen NT2, Leerplan NT2 Richtgraad). No text was copied from them,
and they are not part of this repository. Their publishers and rights: ../THIRD_PARTY.md.

The recordings are not in this folder. They are made from the lessons with the voices listed in ../THIRD_PARTY.md, each
under its own licence.
